Recommends: grass-core | grass,
            rustgis,
Description: run GRASS GIS modules as RustGIS geoprocessing tools
 A RustGIS process plugin that drives the GRASS GIS installed on this machine.
 Vector modules become geoprocessing tools and raster modules become commands
 with a panel of their own:
  - v.voronoi, v.delaunay, v.cluster, v.generalize and v.to.points in the
    Tools pane, with their forms read from the installed GRASS;
  - r.slope.aspect (slope and aspect) and r.viewshed as commands, which export
    the chosen raster layer, run the module and add the result back.
 .
 GRASS itself is neither bundled nor linked: each run spawns the grass
 launcher already on the machine, inside a throwaway database that leaves no
 lock behind. No GRASS code, help text or module description is carried in
 this package; the plugin's manifest is generated from the installation here.
 .
 Run rustgis-grass-setup once after installing, as the user who runs RustGIS.
